1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. O-O {Sindarov allows the Berlin Endgame instead of the Anti-Berlin with 4.d3.} 4... Nxe4 5. d4 Nd6 6. Bxc6 dxc6 7. dxe5 Nf5 8. Qxd8+ Kxd8 9. Rd1+ Ke8 10. Nc3 Ne7 11. h3 Ng6 12. Be3 Be7 13. Ne4 {Sindarov's prepared idea, played quickly.} 13... Bd7 {A new position. Gukesh spent over 15 minutes here.} 14. c4 a5 15. Rd2 a4 16. Rad1 Be6 17. b3 Bb4 {36 minutes. The bishop attacks the rook on d2 and stops White's Nd4 ideas. Gukesh now had 28 minutes against 78.} 18. Re2 h6 19. Ng3 c5 20. Nh5 Rg8 21. g4 {White's best moment has passed. 21.Ne1, heading for d3 or c2, kept a small edge.} (21. Ne1 Nxe5 22. f4 Nc6 23. Nd3) 21... Ke7 22. Ne1 axb3 23. axb3 Nxe5 {Black wins the e5-pawn, but White gets play against the king.} 24. f4 g6 25. Ng3 Nc6 26. f5 gxf5 27. Nxf5+ Kf6 {The only good move.} (27... Bxf5 28. Bg5+ Kf8 29. Bxh6+ Rg7 30. Bxg7+ Kxg7 31. gxf5 {wins the exchange for White.}) 28. Rf2 Rgd8 29. Nd3 Bxf5 30. Rxf5+ Kg7 31. Rh5 Bc3 {Gukesh had under 6 minutes.} 32. Bxh6+ {White wins the pawn back and gives perpetual check.} 32... Kg8 33. Rg5+ Kh7 (33... Bg7 34. Bxg7 Rd6 35. Be5+ {and White is winning.}) 34. Rh5 Kg8 35. Rg5+ Kh7 36. Rh5 Kg8 37. Rg5+ Kh7 38. Rh5 Kg8 1/2-1/2
